;
SWAPPABLE VOLUMES

MOUNT /L lists both J: collections and P: archives.
MOUNT name chooses J: or P: from the image size. Example: MOUNT WALNUT
MOUNT J: /L or MOUNT P: /L lists only the selected catalog.
Use MOUNT J: name or MOUNT P: name if both catalogs share a name.
MOUNT P: /DEFAULT restores SIG/M-CPMUG.
MOUNT J: /DEFAULT restores the startup J: image.
DIR J1: lists J: user area 1. DIR P: lists P: user area 0.

After swapping, MOUNT chains to NDSCAN to refresh directory names.
NDSCAN P: also runs independently. Names come from extensionless -NAME
files in user areas 0-15; areas without markers lose their old names.
Other drives' names and AUTH permissions stay unchanged.
If scanning reports an error, the image is mounted but old names remain.
Use drive/user addresses until the names are corrected or default restored.
Callers need read access to every user area of a drive to scan its names.
Use HELP LIBRARY for archive browsing or HELP GAMES for online play.
